<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Chocolatey NuSpec manifest for Rysh (CLI-only Windows build) -->
<!-- https://community.chocolatey.org -->
<!--
  NOT PUBLISHED. The publish-chocolatey job in .github/workflows/release.yml is
  commented out, and this manifest must not be pushed until someone decides
  whether a CLI-only build belongs in a Windows package manager at all.

  The Windows binary cannot open rysh panes (no ConPTY). Publishing a package
  whose title says "terminal multiplexer" would be false on the one platform
  where it does not multiplex — so the title, summary and description below
  describe the CLI-only build instead.
-->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>rysh</id>
    <version>0.1.0</version>
    <!-- rysh-cli is private and github.com/rysh-ai/rysh does not exist; point
         at what is actually reachable. -->
    <packageSourceUrl>https://rysh.ai/docs</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>rysh-ai</owners>
    <title>Rysh (CLI-only build for Windows)</title>
    <authors>Rysh</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://rysh.ai</projectUrl>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://rysh.ai</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://rysh.ai/docs</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://rysh.ai/docs</bugTrackerUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>cli ai agent development wsl</tags>
    <summary>Command-line client for Rysh. Cannot open panes on Windows — use WSL2 for the multiplexer.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
# Rysh — CLI-only build for Windows

**This package cannot open rysh panes.** Read this before installing.

Rysh is an agentic terminal multiplexer: every pane is a PTY-backed shell that
is also an AI agent. Rysh has no native Windows (ConPTY) PTY implementation, so
a windows/amd64 build links and runs but cannot allocate a terminal. Rather than
fail at the moment you open your first pane, this build refuses session commands
up front.

## What works

```
rysh send <session> <input>   talk to a session running in WSL
rysh install <package>        install an agent from the registry
rysh list-sessions
rysh list-packages
rysh eval
rysh doctor
rysh version
```

## What does not

```
rysh                  (start/attach a session)
rysh <session-name>
rysh attach <name>
rysh create ...
```

These exit immediately with a pointer back to WSL.

## The supported path: WSL2

The Linux build runs unmodified under WSL2, with no rysh-specific configuration:

```powershell
wsl --install
wsl
```

then inside WSL:

```sh
curl -fsSL https://rysh.ai/install.sh | sh
rysh
```

## Native Windows?

It needs a ConPTY implementation behind the existing `internal/platform` seam —
real work, not a flag. It is demand-gated.

## Configuration

Rysh reads `~/.config/rysh/rysh.config.yaml`. Set an Anthropic API key to enable
the agent:

```yaml
provider:
  api_key: "sk-ant-..."
```

Full documentation: https://rysh.ai/docs
    ]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://rysh.ai/docs</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
